# What every Linux package must install into its own lib directory.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# build-deb.sh and build-rpm.sh stage their payloads independently. In 1.7.4
# the rpm turned out to be missing gobbonet-setup.py and wizard.html — the
# first-run setup wizard and its page. The deb staged both; the rpm never had
# them. Nothing noticed, because the spec's %files section globs
# %{_libdir}/gobbonet/* and a glob is happy with whatever it finds.
#
# The user-visible result was a package that installed cleanly and then did
# nothing at all: clicking the icon ran the launcher, the launcher ran
# `python3 $PREFIX/gobbonet-setup.py`, and the file was not there. With the
# desktop entry at Terminal=false and the error dialogs all weak dependencies,
# there was no window, no browser and no message — only a line in
# ~/.local/share/gobbonet/launch.log.
#
# The missing files were the symptom. THE DEFECT WAS TWO LISTS THAT COULD
# DISAGREE, so this is the list, and both builders check themselves against it.
#
# HOW TO CHANGE IT
#
# Adding a file to the payload means adding it here as well. That is the point:
# once it is here, BOTH builds fail until both stage it, so a file can no
# longer arrive on one platform and be forgotten on the other. Removing one is
# the same in reverse.
#
# FORMAT
#
#   name       required; must be present
#   name/      required directory
#   ?name      optional; allowed to be present or absent, never "extra"
#
# Anything staged that is not listed here is an error too. An unexpected file
# is as much a sign of drift as a missing one, and it is usually a leftover
# from an abandoned build.
#
# web/ WAS on this list and was removed in 1.7.5. The chat page is now compiled
# into the gobbonet binary (internal/webui), so a copy on disk is no longer part
# of the payload -- and shipping one would be worse than pointless: the server
# reports an unused web/ beside it at startup so a leftover from an older
# install cannot silently shadow the built-in page, and a packaged copy would
# set that warning off on every launch of a perfectly good install.
#
# It stays off this list rather than becoming optional, because "the package may
# or may not contain a frontend" is exactly the ambiguity this file exists to
# remove.

gobbonet
gobbonet-launch
gobbonet-setup.py
wizard.html
models.ini
llama-cpp/

# Only built when BUNDLE_CPU_ENGINE=1, and only by the deb today. Optional
# rather than required so a normal build is not failed for its absence, and
# not "unlisted" so a CPU build is not failed for its presence.
?llama-cpp-cpu/
